lane: buffer-chunked-feed
why: the last genuine gap -- reading a buffered channel, 264.5us
  against ZStream.fromQueue's 139.1 -- is not the queue (8% of the
  profile) and not Drain. Both SIDES pay a program-as-values step per
  element: `feed` does uncons + async + flatMap + send + flatMap, the
  consumer does uncons + a Free step. Equal cost means the producer
  never runs ahead, the measured batch is 1.67 elements, and chunking
  -- worth 4-7x everywhere else in this library -- cannot engage.
  zio's asymmetry is what gives them 137.9 elements per queue op: a
  cheap q.offer against a consumer paying a Ref update per element.
how: give Channel.buffer a chunk-native feed, so the producer emits
  arrays and the buffer actually fills. feedChunked already exists and
  Channel[Chunk[A]] is already what mergeChunked uses; the piece
  missing is a buffered producer that uses them, plus the chunk-shaped
  read to consume it.
  Land only if the pair beats zioChannelForeach's 139.1; otherwise
  withdraw and record why, as channel-chunks-native was.
